gocontroll-hmi-demo (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop two boot orderings that were never real preconditions. Measured on a
    Moduline HMI1 with systemd-analyze critical-chain, kernel time 1.12s in
    both runs:
    - splash: no longer ordered after systemd-tmpfiles-setup and
      local-fs.target. The asset sits on the root fs and card1 comes from
      devtmpfs, so both only added latency: 3.37s -> 2.68s.
    - demo: no longer ordered after systemd-user-sessions, which pulls in
      network.target and NetworkManager. The Simulink backend, the actual
      precondition, was ready at 1.7s: 5.54s -> 4.48s.
  * Only install signals.json and parameters.json when they are present. Both
    are generated per Simulink build from the .a2l, are gitignored and have
    never been committed, so the unconditional install made dpkg-buildpackage
    fail on every fresh clone. When they are absent src/config.c already falls
    back to addresses derived from the ELF symbols of the bundled
    gocontroll_demo binary.

 -- GOcontroll <info@gocontroll.com>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 14:42:35 +0200

